From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:45:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/58] PROTOTYPE pco: one NaN check for NaN-preserving
 fmin/fmax

pco's min/max are "src0 < src1 ? src0 : src1" (">" for max) in one
instruction group, and a comparison with a NaN operand is false, so a NaN
src0 already gives src1. Only a NaN src1 has to be caught. The lowering
checked both, and each check costs two groups (the boolean is
materialised, then selected on), so a NaN-preserving min/max took five
groups instead of three. GLSL min/max are NaN-preserving since
7e22c43f658, so every clamp() in a GL shader through zink pays this
(Firefox WebRender's YUV shader: 12 per pixel).

Generated-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 4d2cb802c6067c057cac303f0c3cac429b6a6fd5)
(cherry picked from commit 987a47fc811e9ae9fa5f41f4cc0d7ba7f90e6322)
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_alu.c | 13 +++++--------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_alu.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_alu.c
index 25f7a5c5327..58228de839f 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_alu.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_alu.c
@@ -35,10 +35,10 @@ pco_nir_lower_alu_instr(nir_builder *b, nir_alu_instr *alu, void *cb_data)
    switch (alu->op) {
    case nir_op_fmax:
    case nir_op_fmin:
-      /* All hardware comparison instructions return false if any operand is NaN
-       * so a NaN check before is needed.
-       * Directly return the other operand if one of the operands is NaN,
-       * otherwise return the operation result.
+      /* All hardware comparison instructions return false if any operand is NaN.
+       * min/max lower to "src0 < src1 ? src0 : src1" (">" for max), which
+       * therefore already returns src1 when src0 is NaN; only a NaN src1 needs
+       * a check, to return src0 instead.
        */
       if (!nir_alu_instr_is_nan_preserve(alu))
          break;
@@ -51,10 +51,7 @@ pco_nir_lower_alu_instr(nir_builder *b, nir_alu_instr *alu, void *cb_data)
       nir_def *src1_def = nir_ssa_for_alu_src(b, alu, 1);
 
       nir_def *fminmax_nan =
-         nir_bcsel(b,
-                   nir_fisnan(b, src0_def),
-                   src1_def,
-                   nir_bcsel(b, nir_fisnan(b, src1_def), src0_def, &alu->def));
+         nir_bcsel(b, nir_fisnan(b, src1_def), src0_def, &alu->def);
       nir_def_rewrite_uses_after(&alu->def, fminmax_nan);
 
       b->fp_math_ctrl = old_fp_math_ctrl;
